// Declarative realm globals for the Zun base types (PLAN §3.1).
//
// Each line registers a base type onto the realm global as a readonly binding.
// The value identifier (e.g. `Map`) resolves to an opaque class descriptor; the
// registry entry it produces is the single source of truth for how the name
// resolves as a type annotation and how `new <Name>()` lowers, so later a
// program can rebind the surface name (`import Map from "..."`) over the same
// frozen runtime representation.
//
// The compiler recognizes each `global.set("<BaseType>", <BaseType>, true)`
// directive at std-compile time; it is not ordinary executable code (Zun has no
// top-level statements). For now only `Map` flows through this declarative path;
// every other base type stays on the existing hardcoded resolution until it is
// listed here too.

global.set("Map", Map, true);
